We print line numbers so that users can figure out where
the error's coming from.  That's why we don't recommend including
models as quoted strings (also, it rules out either quotes for
printing or the transposition operator depending on which quote you choose).

All of your errors are due to missing constraints in the
parameter declarations.

>     log_d ~ normal(theta_d[1], theta_d[2]);
>     inv_omega ~ beta(theta_o[1], theta_o[2]);

theta_d[2] and theta_o[1] and theta_o[2] all require <lower=0> constraints.
I don't see why you'd put two arguments to normal in the same container,
but you'll have to break them apart to do the constraints.  Same for Dirichlet.

I don't know where <long double> is coming from.  We
shouldn't be using that anywhere.  Are you using 32-bit Windows by any chance?

- Bob

