That's a warning, by the way, not an error.  It can
arise from numerical instability.    The double exp()
is bad news, exp(1 - exp(x)/mu) is very likely to
underflow to zero.

We have an alternative parameterization on the log
scale of neg_binomial_2_log().  That might be more
stable in this case, but you'd have to do some algebra
to get everything onto the log scale.

You can also try to debug it with print() statements to
figure out what the values are and where the zero input
is coming from.

- Bob

